<!--
  Chickadee brand colours — deliberately almost EMPTY since 2026-08-02.

  ## The pivot: one palette, both brands (John)

  Chickadee's brand colour is now the Dashie orange. The right way to express "these two brands
  share a palette" is **no override at all**, not a second copy of the same hex: an override that
  must stay byte-equal to main/ is precisely the hand-mirror standing rule 1 exists to stop, and
  it would drift the first time someone tunes the orange in one place.

  So the whole palette block that used to live here is DELETED rather than re-valued:

    chickadee_blue · orange · dashie_orange{,_light,_dark,_highlight}
    brand_button{,_pressed,_focused} · settings_focus_highlight · chickadee_focus_highlight

  Every one of those names still exists in `main/res/values/colors_settings.xml` and
  `colors.xml`, and every consumer still reads them through the same seam. **The seams are the
  thing that survived** — `@color/brand_button`, the `orange` redirect point, the
  `dashie_full_logo` override machinery. If the brands ever diverge again, re-adding this file
  is a one-file change, which is the property the indirection was bought for.

  ⚠️ Two findings from earlier the same day RESOLVE BY DESIGN and their fixes are gone with the
  block above: the orange Control Center press-animation, and the "Chickadee string with
  Dashie-orange buttons" mixed state. Both were bugs only while the brands had different
  palettes; they are now simply correct. The `values-night/colors.xml` that existed solely to
  win the dark-mode qualifier for `settings_focus_highlight` is deleted for the same reason.

  ## What is still here, and why

  `ic_launcher_background` is about the MARK, not the palette. The orange art landed 2026-08-02
  and the plate stays WHITE: the new mark is an orange waveform-bird on transparent, so an orange
  plate would leave it invisible — the same reason the previous blue-crescent mark needed white,
  arrived at from the opposite direction. The adaptive foreground is the mark alone on
  transparent; background + foreground composite to mark-on-white.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#FFFFFF</color>
</resources>
